A||||4||thomas_l||WOOHOO! It didn't break today!!||||6||
Z||000000||thomas_l||04-29-2001||09:15 PM||||I bought my 87 GT back on 4/4 and the tow truck dropped it in my garage. Over the last few weekends I have been installing an old 4-speed, new clutch, wheel bearings, brake calipers, etc etc etc. Along the way fixing all the cobbled up sh*t done by the last owners. Oh yeah, also got it smogged and registered to boot. Yesterday made the 400 mile round trip to the Fiero Factory - great show & lot of cool folks! And that leads us to...<P><B>Today was race day</B> - SCCA Solo II. <A HREF="http://www.fearlessdata.com/fiero/0429_87GT_AX.wmv" TARGET=_blank>Check out the show</A> I put on in my junkyard rat! OK, so it's Windows Media  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> The stream rate is set at max so it will probably work best if you rt. click and "save as" to view the movie locally (5.7MB). I have heard if you don't have WMP7 or newer you can call it an avi and play it on older versions. I dunno - sorry if it doesn't work. Enjoy!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://fearlessdata.com/fiero/87GT_small.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000001||Old Lar||04-29-2001||11:00 PM||||May be a nice show, but when I clicked on it I got hierogliphic gibberish.||||reg||5
Z||000002||Master_Sushi||04-30-2001||01:45 AM||||Nice driving!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. Looks like you had that GT pushed to the limits. Is it running a stock 2.8?||||reg||14
Z||000003||thomas_l||04-30-2001||09:01 AM||||Yes, it's a stock 2.8 as far as I know. It's a little on the loose side (166k on the odo) but some 5w-50 syntec quieted things down and smoothed it out a good deal. Not to mention the "mystery" oil that was in there had probably aged a good bit  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> while sitting in the repo yard.||||reg||1
Z||000004||thomas_l||04-30-2001||10:02 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Old Lar:<BR><B>May be a nice show, but when I clicked on it I got hierogliphic gibberish.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>As best I can tell from others experience with wmf files, this usually will occur if you just click (i.e. "open") the link and you either don't have Windows Media Player 7 or newer. The browser doesn't know what application to link the wmf extension to so it just assumes HTML and displays the binary data (gibberish). No guarantees, but here's what I have seen work:<BR>1. right-click the link and choose "save-as".<BR>2. The "save-as" dialogue will probably try to call it a *.htm file. Change the extension to wmf and click OK.<BR>3. Once you have it downloaded, click the icon once to highlight.<BR>4. Next, hold the shift key and right click it and choose "run with".<BR>5. Another list will pop up with all your programs - choose whatever you usually watch movies with.<BR>6. If it won't run (i.e. your viewer doesn't know what to do with *.wmf) you might try changing the extension to avi. I heard from someone that did that to view a wmf movie - maybe wmf is a version of avi that Microsoft hinked up enough for a copyright  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
